# Line endings.
#
# Every text file is LF in the repository AND in the working tree, on
# every platform. `eol=lf` is the load-bearing half: without it a
# Windows checkout gets CRLF, and this repository publishes SHA-256
# digests over the RAW BYTES of twenty-six artifacts. A CRLF working
# tree hashes differently from the Linux runner that blessed them, so
# `schema/artifact_manifest.py --check` fails on a clean Windows
# checkout that has nothing wrong with it — and, worse, regenerating to
# "fix" it writes CRLF-derived digests that then fail in CI.
#
# The digests are over raw bytes on purpose: a consumer fetching an
# artifact by URL runs `sha256sum -c`, and a manifest that hashed some
# normalised form would verify something other than what they
# downloaded. So the working tree conforms to the manifest, not the
# other way round.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary. Never examined, never converted.
*.scf   binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.webp  binary
*.zip   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
